# Duplicate profiling PR check

## Overview

Before the **first** `git push` of a branch with no remote, if the
merge-base diff includes Python profiling paths, run the
**`dup-pr-pre-push`** skill. It searches for open, draft, and recently
merged PRs on the same issue, then warns with URLs.

Do not auto-close anything. Do not abandon local work. Skip when the
diff is not profiling.

## Usage

Use the Skill tool with command "dup-pr-pre-push"

Or run the helper directly:

```bash
scripts/search-dup-prs.sh [keyword ...]
```

The helper prints `## scope: skip` and exits 0 when the diff is not
Python profiling. Expanding to all of dd-trace-py is a later flip.

